```

If you could not run a command, say so clearly.

Do not claim something was tested unless it was actually tested.

---

# 12. Do Not Do

Do not:

- Invent major architecture changes
- Add unnecessary frameworks
- Add unnecessary dependencies
- Skip `.env.example`
- Hardcode secrets
- Store sensitive payment or financial data unnecessarily
- Ignore TypeScript errors
- Ignore failing tests
- Delete documentation without replacing it
- Hide assumptions
- Declare work complete without validation notes

---

# 13. Default Definition of Done

A feature is done when:

- It matches the architecture
- It satisfies acceptance criteria
- It has appropriate tests
- It handles errors
- It validates inputs
- It does not expose secrets
- It is documented
- It can run locally
- Known limitations are listed
